IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pip-nouns`

-- SCHEDULE 2 -- MEMBERS OF HER MAJESTY'S FORCES: EXCLUDED PERSONS.
--
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Regulation 19(2) defines "a member of Her Majesty's forces" as a member
-- of the regular or reserve forces other than a person specified in Schedule 2; this module says which
-- persons Schedule 2 specifies. The Schedule's two paragraphs are numbered 1 and 2, but sub-paragraph 1(a)
-- says "subject to paragraph (2)" and paragraph 2 says "Paragraph (1)(a)": both are read as references
-- to paragraphs 2 and 1(a) of this Schedule (fork F-18).

§ `Schedule 2, paragraph 2: the exception to paragraph 1(a)`

-- src:641 | 2 Paragraph (1)(a) does not include any person who –
-- src:642 | (a) has previously been an insured person under Part 1 of the National Insurance Act 1965 ; or
-- src:643 | (b) is paying or has previously paid one or more of the following classes of contributions under the Social Security Act 1975 or the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 –
-- src:644 | (i) primary Class 1;
-- src:645 | (ii) Class 2; or
-- src:646 | (iii) Class 3.
@ref Schedule 2, paragraph 2 (src:641-646)
GIVEN `the person has previously been an insured person under Part 1 of the National Insurance Act 1965` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is paying or has previously paid primary Class 1 contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is paying or has previously paid Class 2 contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is paying or has previously paid Class 3 contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 2: paragraph 1(a) does not include the person` MEANS
       `the person has previously been an insured person under Part 1 of the National Insurance Act 1965`
    OR `the person is paying or has previously paid primary Class 1 contributions`
    OR `the person is paying or has previously paid Class 2 contributions`
    OR `the person is paying or has previously paid Class 3 contributions`

§ `Schedule 2, paragraph 1: persons who are not members of Her Majesty's forces`

-- Sch 2 para 1(a): a person serving as a member of a naval force who locally entered that force at a naval base
-- outside the United Kingdom, subject to paragraph 2.
-- src:637 | 1 The following persons are not members of Her Majesty's forces for the purpose of these Regulations -
-- src:638 | (a) subject to paragraph (2), any person who is serving as a member of any naval force of Her Majesty's forces and who locally entered that force at a naval base outside the United Kingdom;
@ref Schedule 2, paragraph 1(a) (src:637-638)
GIVEN `the person is serving as a member of a naval force of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person locally entered that force at a naval base outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph 1(a) does not include the person, by paragraph 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 1(a): the person is not a member of Her Majesty's forces as a locally entered naval person` MEANS
        `the person is serving as a member of a naval force of Her Majesty's forces`
    AND `the person locally entered that force at a naval base outside the United Kingdom`
    AND (NOT `paragraph 1(a) does not include the person, by paragraph 2`)

-- Sch 2 para 1(b): a person serving as a member of a military force who entered that force, or was recruited
-- for it, outside the United Kingdom, and the depot of whose unit is outside the United Kingdom.
-- src:639 | (b) any person who is serving as a member of any military force of Her Majesty's forces and who entered that force, or was recruited for that force, outside the United Kingdom, and the depot of whose unit is situated outside the United Kingdom;
@ref Schedule 2, paragraph 1(b) (src:639)
GIVEN `the person is serving as a member of a military force of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person entered that force, or was recruited for it, outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the depot of the person's unit is outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 1(b): the person is not a member of Her Majesty's forces as a military person recruited abroad` MEANS
        `the person is serving as a member of a military force of Her Majesty's forces`
    AND `the person entered that force, or was recruited for it, outside the United Kingdom`
    AND `the depot of the person's unit is outside the United Kingdom`

-- Sch 2 para 1(c): a person serving as a member of an air force who entered that force, or was recruited for it,
-- outside the United Kingdom, and is liable under the terms of engagement to serve only in a specified part of
-- the world outside the United Kingdom.
-- src:640 | (c) any person who is serving as a member of any air force of Her Majesty's forces and who entered that force, or was recruited for that force, outside the United Kingdom, and is liable under the terms of engagement to serve only in a specified part of the world outside the United Kingdom.
@ref Schedule 2, paragraph 1(c) (src:640)
GIVEN `the person is serving as a member of an air force of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person entered that air force, or was recruited for it, outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is liable under the terms of engagement to serve only in a specified part of the world outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 1(c): the person is not a member of Her Majesty's forces as an air force person recruited abroad` MEANS
        `the person is serving as a member of an air force of Her Majesty's forces`
    AND `the person entered that air force, or was recruited for it, outside the United Kingdom`
    AND `the person is liable under the terms of engagement to serve only in a specified part of the world outside the United Kingdom`

-- Sch 2 para 1: the person is within sub-paragraph (a), (b) or (c). A person who is within none of them is
-- not specified in the Schedule and so can be a member of Her Majesty's forces under regulation 19(2).
-- src:637 | 1 The following persons are not members of Her Majesty's forces for the purpose of these Regulations -
@ref Schedule 2, paragraph 1 (src:637)
GIVEN `the person is within paragraph 1(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is within paragraph 1(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is within paragraph 1(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 1: the person is specified in Schedule 2` MEANS
       `the person is within paragraph 1(a)`
    OR `the person is within paragraph 1(b)`
    OR `the person is within paragraph 1(c)`
